  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    import numpy as np\n    g = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    rows, cols = len(g), len(g[0])\n    \n    # Find 2-cells (the frame)\n    twos = [(r,c) for r in range(rows) for c in range(cols) if g[r][c] == 2]\n    # Find 5-cells\n    fives = [(r,c) for r in range(rows) for c in range(cols) if g[r][c] == 5]\n    \n    if not twos or not fives:\n        return g\n    \n    # Bounding box of 2s\n    min_r2 = min(r for r,c in twos)\n    max_r2 = max(r for r,c in twos)\n    min_c2 = min(c for r,c in twos)\n    max_c2 = max(c for r,c in twos)\n    \n    # Find the opening/interior bounds\n    # The interior is bounded by the 2-frame\n    \n    # For each group of 5s, determine which side they're on and reflect inward\n    # Clear all 5s first\n    out = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    for r,c in fives:\n        out[r][c] = 0\n    \n    # Determine reflection for each 5-cell\n    for r,c in fives:\n        # Determine which side relative to the 2-box\n        if r < min_r2:  # above\n            new_r = min_r2 + (min_r2 - r)\n            new_c = c\n        elif r > max_r2:  # below\n            new_r = max_r2 - (r - max_r2)\n            new_c = c\n        elif c < min_c2:  # left\n            new_r = r\n            new_c = min_c2 + (min_c2 - c)\n        elif c > max_c2:  # right\n            new_r = r\n            new_c = max_c2 - (c - max_c2)\n        else:\n            new_r, new_c = r, c\n        \n        if 0 <= new_r < rows and 0 <= new_c < cols:\n            out[new_r][new_c] = 5\n    \n    return out\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    import numpy as np\n    g = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    rows, cols = len(g), len(g[0])\n    \n    # Find 2-cells (the frame)\n    twos = [(r,c) for r in range(rows) for c in range(cols) if g[r][c] == 2]\n    # Find 5-cells\n    fives = [(r,c) for r in range(rows) for c in range(cols) if g[r][c] == 5]\n    \n    if not twos or not fives:\n        return g\n    \n    # Bounding box of 2s\n    min_r2 = min(r for r,c in twos)\n    max_r2 = max(r for r,c in twos)\n    min_c2 = min(c for r,c in twos)\n    max_c2 = max(c for r,c in twos)\n    \n    # Find the opening/interior bounds\n    # The interior is bounded by the 2-frame\n    \n    # For each group of 5s, determine which side they're on and reflect inward\n    # Clear all 5s first\n    out = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    for r,c in fives:\n        out[r][c] = 0\n    \n    # Determine reflection for each 5-cell\n    for r,c in fives:\n        # Determine which side relative to the 2-box\n        if r < min_r2:  # above\n            new_r = min_r2 + (min_r2 - r)\n            new_c = c\n        elif r > max_r2:  # below\n            new_r = max_r2 - (r - max_r2)\n            new_c = c\n        elif c < min_c2:  # left\n            new_r = r\n            new_c = min_c2 + (min_c2 - c)\n        elif c > max_c2:  # right\n            new_r = r\n            new_c = max_c2 - (c - max_c2)\n        else:\n            new_r, new_c = r, c\n        \n        if 0 <= new_r < rows and 0 <= new_c < cols:\n            out[new_r][new_c] = 5\n    \n    return out",
